  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 203 PM MDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nMonday Night - Saturday: For the rest of the forecast period, active \nweather continues for south central and southeastern Colorado, \nthough with a downtick in activity heading into the later part of \nthe week. The stubborn high pressure will remain in place through at \nleast the first half of the week, bringing additional abundant \nmoisture. This moisture, along with any vort maxes and short waves, \nwill bring additional days with afternoon and evening showers and \nstorms, with the greatest coverage Tuesday and Wednesday. Then \nheading into the later part of the week, the high pressure is \nexpected to drift southward and flatten out. This will eventually \ncut-off the deeper moisture tap, with showers and storms decreasing \nin coverage past Wednesday, but especially Friday and Saturday. \nOtherwise, winds continue to remain relatively light, with increased \ncloud cover expected each afternoon. As for temperatures, while a \ndip is expected midweek, temperatures remain warm and mostly above \nseasonal values, especially heading into next weekend.",
